1
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,199
(Episode 6)

2
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,960
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:54,760
What's going on? How long do we have to wait?

4
00:01:54,920 --> 00:01:56,920
How much longer?

5
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,840
Has anyone seen this ghost?

6
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,880
There's a reward for whoever finds him.

7
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:10,400
- A reward? - Who is he?

8
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:14,960
Please help us. There's money in it.

9
00:02:15,280 --> 00:02:16,640
Keep an eye out for this ghost.

10
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,840
Thank you.

11
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,280
Please keep an eye out.

12
00:02:22,280 --> 00:02:24,080
Tell us if you see this male ghost.

13
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,200
Are you trying to cut in line?

14
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,920
Don't act like you don't know.

15
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The end of the line is back there.

16
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:32,080
I just want to know what you're lining up for.

17
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:34,040
To be reincarnated. Get in line.

18
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:36,440
How long have you been waiting?

19
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:39,440
Decades. I should be seeing my hometown soon.

20
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,040
My wish is to find a rich ghost...

21
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,840
to buy me a VIP pass.

22
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:49,000
Looks like my son died too.

23
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,760
Another one who couldn't wait.

24
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:56,440
But it's for the best.

25
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,880
He waited for over 20 years.

26
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,000
At least his son was filial.

27
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:02,280
Many ghosts here just dissipate after waiting a short while.

28
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:09,080
Has anyone seen them?

29
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:11,160
Have you seen them?

30
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,360
If you have, I can pay you.

31
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,000
They look so ordinary. How can anyone recognize them?

32
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,880
I've been waiting so long and haven't seen them.

33
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:38,600
(Looking for Chiu Wing Tai, male, in his sixties, from Hong Kong)

34
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:46,080
Any news?

35
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,840
No. Should I keep handing these out?

36
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,440
There's no time.

37
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,959
If they really think I'm dead and burn my body,

38
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,720
then I'll be stuck here forever.

39
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,840
I must visit Senior and Ben in a dream...

40
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,080
and tell them not to cremate me.

41
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,720
I know where Chiu Wing Tai is.

42
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:23,040
Is Chiu Wing Tai really here?

43
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,440
His resentment is so deep that he became a malicious ghost.

44
00:04:25,720 --> 00:04:27,240
That's why he's stuck here.

45
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,600
Can you slow down?

46
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,240
Where's Chiu Wing Tai?

47
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,960
Why won't you let me go even though I'm a ghost?

48
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,720
Why won't you let me go even in death?

49
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,800
I just want to apologize to you.

50
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,200
I hope you can forgive me.

51
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,720
You helped that jerk trick my wife.

52
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:31,680
You ruined my family business.

53
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:34,000
Three generations of the Chiu family were ruined by your hands.

54
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,000
Dying 10 times wouldn't atone for your sins.

55
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:37,120
How dare you ask for my forgiveness?

56
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,480
Give me another chance.

57
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,800
I can make things right.

58
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,120
Please give me another chance.

59
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:42,960
Let me return to the mortal realm.

60
00:05:42,961 --> 00:05:44,720
I can handle everything for you.

61
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,640
I just helped Shek Chung fulfill his last wish.

62
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:48,560
I can help you get all your assets back!

63
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,280
Shut up!

64
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,600
You showed those videos to my wife.

65
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:56,440
The damage is irreversible.

66
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,880
My wife was the person who treated me best.

67
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:00,640
After what you did to her,

68
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:02,600
there's no way to make amends!

69
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,240
It's you.

70
00:06:05,480 --> 00:06:08,520
You're the one who ruined me, leaving me unable to die in peace!

71
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:11,400
Blood for blood!

72
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,240
What's going on?

73
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:48,960
I recognize you.

74
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,680
You're that scumbag lawyer.

75
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:52,680
I don't know you. Let me go!

76
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,920
You don't recognize me?

77
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,280
I'm To Wing Kiu.

78
00:06:57,440 --> 00:07:00,200
You defended that murderer, Yip Chau Wong.

79
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,879
(To Wing Kiu)

80
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,800
My brother was sued for intimidation by that scumbag.

81
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,640
He's in prison now.

82
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,160
My mother fell ill from grief and never recovered.

83
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:11,920
My father got injured at work trying to pay the legal fees.

84
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,960
You ruined my entire family!

85
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:19,080
Justice is served. You're dead now.

86
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,200
You can't hurt anyone else.

87
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,360
I want you to rot in the 18th level of hell!

88
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:24,240
I want you to never be reincarnated!

89
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,040
Did you turn Tai into this?

90
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:33,960
Resentment is like a drug.

91
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,120
It makes you stronger.

92
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,560
It turns you into a powerful, malicious ghost.

93
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,680
But toxins accumulate in the body.

94
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:42,760
When resentment grows too deep to be resolved,

95
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:45,440
it backfires and leads to self-destruction.

96
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:49,520
But if he had let go of his resentment toward you,

97
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,800
he could have reincarnated and atoned for his sins,

98
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,640
instead of being shattered into pieces.

99
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,080
Now do you understand why your lifespan was shortened so much?

100
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:02,320
What you did didn't just hurt the victims.

101
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:06,080
It caused equal pain to everyone around them.

102
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,240
You didn't think it would be this serious, right?

103
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,320
I want to stay in the mortal realm for a while longer.

104
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,440
If it's not enough, I'll burn more.

105
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:22,320
You can have as much as you want.

106
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:27,280
Do you really think I'm not letting you return for money?

107
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,720
Let me ask you again.

108
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,320
Why don't you want to die? What do you want to go back for?

109
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,680
You're so disappointed in people anyway.

110
00:08:32,760 --> 00:08:34,720
You think they're greedy and use you.

111
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:35,880
Why don't you just let it go?

112
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:39,680
Being a cat or dog in your next life is better than being human.

113
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:48,280
I still have a lot of questions that I want answers to.

114
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,200
Let me go back to the mortal world.

115
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:53,160
I promise I won't hurt anyone again.

116
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:54,720
There's only one rule.

117
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,400
Karma.

118
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,400
Look at your arm.

119
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,720
Roll up your sleeve higher.

120
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
What is this?

121
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,320
Haven't you always wanted to know...

122
00:09:14,321 --> 00:09:15,760
how much longer you have to live?

123
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:19,040
When this line reaches your heart, you'll die.

124
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:21,960
Your lifespan was supposed to be 70.

125
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:23,360
After the deduction, only 31 remains.

126
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,200
If you really want to stay longer,

127
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,680
you have to do some genuinely good deeds.

128
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,800
Accumulate virtue, and this line will shorten.

129
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:36,640
So if I do good deeds, will this line get shorter?

130
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:39,320
Then I don't have to pay you.

131
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,240
No, those are two different things.

132
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:42,720
I can do that.

133
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,640
But whether I do it or not is up to me.

134
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,920
So I don't have to die in two days?

135
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,720
If you accumulate enough virtue.

136
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,720
What's the best way to accumulate virtue?

137
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,560
Donate money? Blood? Volunteer?

138
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:05,520
Is this utilitarianism just a habit,

139
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,160
or is your nature hard to change?

140
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:14,000
If you keep trying to earn virtue with this mindset,

141
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,080
we'll meet again very soon.

142
00:10:31,320 --> 00:10:32,520
Are you Yau Yam Yam?

143
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,760
- What is it? - How did you return to the living?

144
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:38,000
Yeah, what's your secret?

145
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,720
I'm in a hurry.

146
00:10:39,721 --> 00:10:41,640
What did you do to make the King of Hell let you return?

147
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:44,160
Tell me. I can give you a lot of money.

148
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,560
I can give you these coins too.

149
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,120
- Take them. Take these first. - Teach me how to return to life.

150
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,320
This is it. It can bring me back to the mortal world.

151
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,320
- Stop! - Don't go!

152
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:09,080
31, 32, 33, 34, 35,

153
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:11,520
36, 37, 38, 39, 40,

154
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:15,000
11, 12, 13, 14, 15,

155
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,240
16, 17, 18, 19, 20,

156
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,560
21, 22, 23, 23, 24, 25,

157
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:22,040
26, 27, 28, 29, 30,

158
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:25,120
31, 32, 33, 34, 35, 36...

159
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,640
Death confirmed.

160
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:32,360
Time of death is 12:36pm.

161
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,240
Again?

162
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,240
Are you okay?

163
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:01,840
- Are you all right? - Wake up.

164
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,920
There's nothing wrong with you physically.

165
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,240
But why did this happen?

166
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,480
Can I be discharged now?

167
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:20,800
Yes, but your heart stopped for quite a while.

168
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:23,200
I suggest you have a check-up later.

169
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:24,840
Thank you, doctor.

170
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Are you okay?

171
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:58,320
That woman has been arrested.

172
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,200
She won't say a word.

173
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,880
We found a black outfit and a helmet at her place.

174
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:05,240
The police will charge her with attempted murder.

175
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:10,520
Bill the medical expenses to me.

176
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,640
Everything is packed.

177
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,720
Are you going home now?

178
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:35,760
Mrs. Chiu.

179
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,560
Mrs. Chiu, I have something to tell you.

180
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,040
Just listen to what she has to say.

181
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:49,760
Leaving everything to you...

182
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,760
was Tai's last wish.

183
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,840
You were the one who treated him best.

184
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:58,640
He wanted to apologize to you.

185
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,040
He hoped you would forgive him.

186
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,280
I shouldn't have helped Jeffrey.

187
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,320
But now that he's dead,

188
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,640
I want to help you settle the estate.

189
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,360
I can help you get everything back.

190
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,040
I don't care about the money at all.

191
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:32,400
People like you will never understand.

192
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,360
You can go now.

193
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,399
(To Wing Kiu)

194
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:15,679
(Female Victim's Brother Arrested...)

195
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,520
(After Causing a Disturbance at Leather Tycoon's Mansion)

196
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:23,160
Have you been there too?

197
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,240
Where?

198
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,800
Did you see the King of Hell too?

199
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,400
Did you also return from the dead?

200
00:15:38,400 --> 00:15:39,880
Actually, I've been down there too.

201
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:44,720
Strictly speaking,

202
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:48,120
it was my mom who dragged me down there.

203
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,240
The food is ready.

204
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:05,440
How did you know I wanted an all-day breakfast?

205
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:07,480
Hurry up. Go brush your teeth first.

206
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,560
Mom, I'll show you something after we eat.

207
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,240
A birthday present?

208
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:17,400
Great, I love getting presents!

209
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:35,160
Are you ready?

210
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,239
Happy birthday!

211
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,320
Your son spent a long time looking for this.

212
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,800
He had it shipped here from Japan.

213
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,280
Good boy!

214
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:51,160
What are you waiting for?

215
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:57,880
Mom.

216
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,440
Son.

217
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,160
Will you stay with me wherever I go?

218
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,320
Of course. Where do you want to go?

219
00:17:34,840 --> 00:17:36,600
I'm so happy on my birthday today.

220
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:39,080
Thank you.

221
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:47,120
I want to be with you forever.

222
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,280
Being this happy every day.

223
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,960
With nothing to worry about.

224
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,560
Mom, slow down.

225
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,000
It's dangerous.

226
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,600
Let me drive. I'll drive.

227
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,360
Slow down!

228
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:21,280
Mom, where are we?

229
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:23,560
We're together now.

230
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:25,440
We don't have to be afraid anywhere.

231
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:29,760
Stand still.

232
00:18:32,280 --> 00:18:34,320
What is your name?

233
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,200
Kam Yin Pan.

234
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,760
It's not his time yet.

235
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,040
Why did you drag him down?

236
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,360
We were supposed to bring Lui Ching Han down.

237
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:00,440
But look at her, she's dragging Kam Yin Pan down with her.

238
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,480
And his time was almost up anyway.

239
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:04,560
So we just took him too.

240
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,800
- Yes, it was an accident. - Shut up!

241
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,280
Always with these excuses.

242
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,440
How many times has this been?

243
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:12,799
You're always so sloppy with your work.

244
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,840
Still playing innocent?

245
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:17,400
Believe it or not, I'll make you work like beasts of burden.

246
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:18,480
Please don't, my lord.

247
00:19:18,600 --> 00:19:19,640
Forgive me.

248
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:21,320
We won't dare do it again.

249
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,800
You really deserve a scolding.

250
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,240
Send him back now. What are you waiting for?

251
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:29,320
Yes, my lord!

252
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,680
Don't take him away!

253
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,800
We... We're supposed to be together!

254
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,400
You've committed the grave sin of suicide.

255
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,800
- You want to take your son too? - No!

256
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:37,840
Kneel right now! I'm going to interrogate you.

257
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:40,360
- Mom. - Ben!

258
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:43,720
Ben!

259
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:47,760
Come back! Don't take him away!

260
00:20:28,280 --> 00:20:30,160
Did your mother ever visit you after that?

261
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:35,160
Did she appear in your dreams?

262
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:38,840
No.

263
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,960
I really want to see her again.

264
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,360
I want to ask her how she's doing.

265
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,800
And why she did what she did.

266
00:20:58,600 --> 00:20:59,960
I'm glad you're back.

267
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:02,600
Did Ox Head and Horse Face make another mistake?

268
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:09,880
I'm not supposed to be here.

269
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:14,520
I've done too many bad things, shortening my lifespan.

270
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,760
But the King of Hell gave me one extra chance.

271
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:25,640
If this line reaches my heart, I'll die.

272
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:28,920
I only have two days left.

273
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:32,680
If I can do more good deeds and accumulate merit,

274
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:35,360
I might be able to live a bit longer.

275
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:41,000
So that's why you burned joss paper for yourself...

276
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:44,240
and wrote a to-do list.

277
00:21:47,960 --> 00:21:49,320
Because you knew you were leaving?

278
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,280
I had to make some preparations.

279
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:10,200
Because I know that after I die,

280
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:14,320
no one will remember me.

281
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,600
No one will burn offerings for me.

282
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:25,120
I'll remember you.

283
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:01,280
Thank you.

284
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,040
But I'm out of time.

285
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:12,400
I don't want to use you to escape my feelings anymore.

286
00:23:22,760 --> 00:23:23,760
Hello?

287
00:23:27,640 --> 00:23:29,080
Okay, I'm coming back now.

288
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:33,120
I'll give you a ride.

289
00:23:39,480 --> 00:23:41,120
Alan said your car is ready for pickup.

290
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,600
What's wrong?

291
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:44,280
It won't start.

292
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:46,760
I wonder if it's related to the accident last time.

293
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,200
Actually, I'm curious sometimes.

294
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:54,840
What kind of men do you like?

295
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:04,360
I don't know.

296
00:24:07,440 --> 00:24:08,600
Maybe I feel like...

297
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:12,080
I don't have to pretend when I'm with him.

298
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,760
Or maybe because he's richer than me,

299
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,760
I feel his kindness isn't for my money.

300
00:24:23,080 --> 00:24:24,680
I always tell you I won't take your money.

301
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:26,840
But you're the one who insists.

302
00:24:29,920 --> 00:24:32,080
I'm happy to hear your sweet talk.

303
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:34,720
I think it's worth it.

304
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:36,960
What sweet talk?

305
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,320
I'm being serious.

306
00:24:45,520 --> 00:24:46,800
Actually, you don't need a reason...

307
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:50,000
to like someone.

308
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:55,960
I totally agree.

309
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:04,320
I think I'll call a car.

310
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,920
I want to be alone for a bit.

311
00:25:36,960 --> 00:25:37,960
Hello?

312
00:25:40,960 --> 00:25:42,040
Okay, I'm coming over now.

313
00:25:57,280 --> 00:25:58,280
What's the matter?

314
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:11,240
They've decided to push me to be the chairman.

315
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,000
The committee is all on their side.

316
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:18,240
So I'll definitely be elected.

317
00:26:23,240 --> 00:26:26,200
Being chairman now makes me a target.

318
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:28,720
My wife thinks...

319
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,920
I can take over her father's position.

320
00:26:33,920 --> 00:26:36,160
Why turn down such a good thing?

321
00:26:38,520 --> 00:26:39,960
She said I don't know how to cherish it.

322
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:44,360
She doesn't understand what I want.

323
00:26:51,080 --> 00:26:52,360
In the end, she found out.

324
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,760
She kept crying.

325
00:27:05,800 --> 00:27:07,520
She said she can't accept...

326
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:10,000
a drug-addicted husband.

327
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:16,440
She said she was disappointed in me.

328
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,880
I'm no longer the perfect Yeung Kam Tsuen...

329
00:27:21,640 --> 00:27:23,360
she had in mind.

330
00:27:24,600 --> 00:27:26,040
She wants a divorce.

331
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:32,560
Then get a divorce.

332
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:38,160
If we divorce,

333
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:40,000
her father will definitely find out.

334
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:41,080
He won't let me off the hook.

335
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:43,360
I won't even be able to be a lawyer then.

336
00:27:46,520 --> 00:27:47,680
Then don't be one.

337
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:52,320
Didn't you say you wanted to change?

338
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:07,680
Give me some time.

339
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:37,480
Do you really not find me attractive?

340
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:40,600
That's not it.

341
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:43,160
It's the rule.

342
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:52,520
Isn't it more affectionate just to hug like this?

343
00:29:57,360 --> 00:30:01,040
Is there any client you can't resist?

344
00:30:11,520 --> 00:30:12,680
You should leave him.

345
00:30:13,760 --> 00:30:15,160
He won't let me go.

346
00:30:15,960 --> 00:30:17,400
He just wants to torture me.

347
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:22,760
If you want,

348
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:25,320
I can help you.

349
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:28,600
I don't believe he can find you no matter where you go.

350
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:35,320
Don't worry, no extra charge.

351
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,400
What are you doing?

352
00:30:46,600 --> 00:30:47,600
Don't do anything stupid.

353
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,360
Hey!

354
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:52,400
Let go!

355
00:30:53,240 --> 00:30:54,240
Wench.

356
00:30:57,240 --> 00:30:58,240
Let go of her!

357
00:30:59,120 --> 00:31:00,120
Hooking up?

358
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:01,720
Wench, you're cheating?

359
00:31:05,520 --> 00:31:06,520
Darn it!

360
00:31:10,680 --> 00:31:12,200
Don't hit him so hard.

361
00:31:12,680 --> 00:31:14,280
I have something good for him.

362
00:31:28,640 --> 00:31:29,640
Honey.

363
00:31:31,080 --> 00:31:32,240
Changed your taste?

364
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:36,560
You like slick boys whose hair hasn't even grown in?

365
00:31:40,040 --> 00:31:41,320
How dare you mess with my woman?

366
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:00,640
What's the matter?

367
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:03,720
You have to help me.

368
00:32:05,320 --> 00:32:06,320
Help you with what?

369
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:08,000
Help me with a lawsuit.

370
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:09,560
What?

371
00:32:12,080 --> 00:32:13,080
Come in.

372
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:18,320
Breakfast?

373
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:33,920
Are you okay?

374
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,400
Is the breakfast okay?

375
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,400
It's okay.

376
00:32:43,960 --> 00:32:45,440
You said you needed time.

377
00:32:47,400 --> 00:32:48,400
How long?

378
00:32:52,680 --> 00:32:54,640
At least till I end my last relationship first.

379
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,440
I'm rather traditional.

380
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:08,360
I need to change step by step.

381
00:33:13,560 --> 00:33:15,280
I have a meeting. I'll call you later.

382
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:36,360
Hello?

383
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:39,600
I'll send you a list of names later.

384
00:33:39,680 --> 00:33:41,080
You and Senior investigate them for me.

385
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,040
Don't do anything else. Just do this.

386
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:46,360
Can't find her?

387
00:33:47,360 --> 00:33:49,400
If you can't find her, do it yourself.

388
00:33:49,560 --> 00:33:50,760
Check as many as you can.

389
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:52,799
Also, I want info...

390
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:54,120
on all the non-profit organizations in the world.

391
00:33:54,880 --> 00:33:55,880
Hurry.

392
00:34:01,640 --> 00:34:02,680
Didn't Ben call you?

393
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:05,480
Yes, he told me to pick up the car.

394
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:07,760
No, didn't Ben ask you to bail him out?

395
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,520
- Bail him out? - He was charged with rape.

396
00:34:12,640 --> 00:34:13,800
Explain that to me.

397
00:34:14,120 --> 00:34:15,920
I told him she was Dee's woman.

398
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,200
I told him to stay away.

399
00:34:18,120 --> 00:34:20,280
He didn't listen, and now he's in trouble.

400
00:34:20,840 --> 00:34:23,720
Dee? Hung Shing's Dee?

401
00:34:24,880 --> 00:34:26,200
Ben touched his woman?

402
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:29,000
Yes. Now he's being set up.

403
00:34:30,240 --> 00:34:32,840
If I had stopped him earlier, this wouldn't have happened.

404
00:34:33,040 --> 00:34:34,560
But he just wouldn't listen.

405
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:37,560
He always says he can't bear to see any woman unhappy.

406
00:34:37,800 --> 00:34:39,240
Isn't he crazy?

407
00:34:52,280 --> 00:34:53,360
Why are you here?

408
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:57,120
Rape? And you're pleading guilty?

409
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:00,440
If I don't confess, he might kill his wife.

410
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:03,440
Are you sure he won't kill her if you confess?

411
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:05,560
How old are you? You're so naive.

412
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:07,240
I know Dee. He's insane.

413
00:35:09,960 --> 00:35:12,320
Don't worry, we really didn't do it.

414
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:14,920
They have no evidence. I'll be out soon.

415
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:17,040
You've confessed. What more evidence do they need?

416
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,680
He wants you in prison so he can have you killed inside.

417
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:21,560
Even one day in there is too long.

418
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:27,400
Then can you bail me out?

419
00:35:28,120 --> 00:35:29,840
How can I? It's a rape charge, and you confessed.

420
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:35,160
Can't you say I was misled...

421
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:37,320
or threatened into confessing?

422
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:40,240
You must have a way.

423
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:43,120
I was framed. Helping me is a good deed.

424
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:45,400
Maybe it will shorten that line.

425
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:55,760
Then do as I say.

426
00:36:17,240 --> 00:36:18,800
Add this case to the schedule.

427
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:22,840
Rape?

428
00:36:24,280 --> 00:36:26,120
- Did you find it? - What?

429
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,600
The info on our former opponents and the NGOs.

430
00:36:30,640 --> 00:36:31,640
Yes.

431
00:36:42,640 --> 00:36:43,640
Is that all?

432
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,400
I could find this online myself.

433
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:50,440
I haven't found Senior yet.

434
00:36:54,720 --> 00:36:56,560
Let's go. Time is running out.

435
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,000
Who are we looking for?

436
00:37:13,001 --> 00:37:14,800
Hello, I'm looking for Ms. Chiu Man Wah.

437
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:18,680
What are you doing here?

438
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:21,320
I want to see how I can help you.

439
00:37:21,600 --> 00:37:23,680
It's her. She told the security guard not to testify.

440
00:37:23,760 --> 00:37:24,920
She's the reason I lost everything.

441
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:28,680
So you're that awful lawyer!

442
00:37:28,760 --> 00:37:29,760
Please calm down.

443
00:37:30,000 --> 00:37:32,160
I know I was wrong. I can pay you.

444
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:33,400
You think money is everything?

445
00:37:33,480 --> 00:37:36,200
Do you know my daughter can't work because of you?

446
00:37:36,280 --> 00:37:37,920
- She's a laughingstock! - Leave, scumbag!

447
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:39,720
I don't want your money!

448
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:40,840
I'll hit you every time I see you!

449
00:37:40,920 --> 00:37:42,640
Don't let me see you again!

450
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:53,519
Hello, I'm the legal representative for Tam Sang Real Estate.

451
00:37:53,520 --> 00:37:54,520
Tam Sang Real Estate?

452
00:37:54,521 --> 00:37:56,760
You're the jerk who made me homeless!

453
00:37:56,840 --> 00:37:58,680
I'm sorry, I want...

454
00:38:03,880 --> 00:38:04,880
Hello.

455
00:38:04,881 --> 00:38:06,640
I'm Yau Yam Yam, Wong Man Na's lawyer.

456
00:38:06,720 --> 00:38:08,720
Wong Man Na? How dare you come?

457
00:38:08,800 --> 00:38:10,040
You're the reason I'm in this state!

458
00:38:10,120 --> 00:38:11,640
- What do you want? Get lost! - I'm sorry.

459
00:38:11,720 --> 00:38:13,680
I don't want to see you! Don't go, I'm not done with you yet!

460
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:15,440
You ruined my life, and I'm not done scolding you!

461
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:18,480
They won't listen or take money.

462
00:38:18,800 --> 00:38:20,480
I really don't understand why people are so stubborn.

463
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:23,440
It's not stubbornness. They just can't let it go.

464
00:38:24,160 --> 00:38:25,880
Even if they can't let it go,

465
00:38:25,960 --> 00:38:27,960
they could at least take the money first.

466
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:30,240
Think of it as letting me do something for them.

467
00:38:30,920 --> 00:38:33,280
Maybe you can't give them what they really want.

468
00:38:36,280 --> 00:38:37,840
The mistake has been made.

469
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:40,680
They should at least take the money.

470
00:38:46,840 --> 00:38:48,920
Why do you suddenly want to do something for them?

471
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:54,000
To make yourself feel better?

472
00:38:56,080 --> 00:38:57,080
It's a win-win.

473
00:39:00,400 --> 00:39:01,640
I feel a bit better,

474
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,680
and they get some compensation.

475
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:08,320
Money is always useful.

476
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:09,800
At least it makes people a bit happier.

477
00:39:12,800 --> 00:39:13,800
Is that so?

478
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:16,280
Of course.

479
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:18,920
I have my reservations.

480
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:31,200
Amber, I just took on a few very good cases.

481
00:39:31,280 --> 00:39:32,280
They're perfect for you.

482
00:39:32,440 --> 00:39:33,840
I don't want to take any cases lately.

483
00:39:34,640 --> 00:39:36,320
Just take a look. They really are perfect for you.

484
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:44,800
I can't take these cases.

485
00:39:45,960 --> 00:39:46,960
Why not?

486
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:48,840
Fatal accidents, suing small business owners,

487
00:39:48,920 --> 00:39:50,239
and a son suing his father.

488
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:51,399
How can I take these?

489
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:52,440
Why can't you?

490
00:39:52,520 --> 00:39:54,360
You've always handled these types of cases.

491
00:39:59,880 --> 00:40:01,080
Help me join the Legal Aid panel.

492
00:40:02,280 --> 00:40:03,280
What?

493
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:05,920
Are you joking?

494
00:40:08,360 --> 00:40:09,760
Do you know how much Legal Aid pays?

495
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,560
A whole case isn't even as much...

496
00:40:11,640 --> 00:40:12,840
as your consultation fee for three hours.

497
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:18,560
Anyway, I'm only doing Legal Aid now.

498
00:40:31,920 --> 00:40:32,920
Master...
